 "notes": "The list runs over pp. 54–55: n69.jpg has the heading and stations 81–90, and n70.jpg has stations 91–114. n67 is p. 52 (running text). The page numbers show that n68 and n71 fall before and after the list, so I didn't open them. Every row was clear in the scan, so no row is marked unsure.\n\nHow the table is laid out:\n- **Columns:** \"Returns in 8 years, including 1887.\" | \"In 1887.\" (holds only the * marks) | number and station | \"Values.\" | \"Feet.\" The headings say 1887 even though this is the 1886 report, because returns ran to Feb. 1887. In each \"other\" field I give the 8-year count first, then the value, then the height, separated by \" | \". I shortened the dot leaders to \"...\".\n- **Sub-headings:** \"SUTHERLAND.\" covers 81–82. \"OUTER HEBRIDES.\" covers 83–90, and on p. 55 it carries on as \"OUTER HEBRIDES—_continued._\" over 91–114. So mainland and Clyde/Galloway stations (Corran Ferry through Little Ross) are printed under that heading too. I've copied the printed grouping, not corrected it.\n- **No keepers:** none are named in the list. A sideways note in the margin of both pages reads: \"The names of the Reporters are given under \"Diary from the Stations.\"\" The keepers will have to come from that Diary section, which starts lower on p. 55.\n- **Totals check:** there are 35 stations (81–114 plus 109b) and 15 carry a * (83, 86, 89, 90, 93, 94, 101, 102, 103, 108, 109, 110, 112, 113, 114). Both match the lead-in: schedules sent to \"thirty-five stations\" and returns from \"fifteen stations\".\n- **Braces:** for 84 Stornoway and 86 Monach Islands, the \"brace\" in marks is the brace printed round the paired values (and, for Stornoway, round the single height). It doesn't group stations. Stornoway is \"{ II. / I. }\" with one height, 56. Monach Islands is \"{ I. / II. }\" with heights 150 and 62. I put \"(2 Lights)\" in Stornoway's \"other\", not its name.\n- **109b:** the number is printed \"109B.\" with the B as a small capital. Its row reads \"Ailsa Craig, 1885,\" with no value or height; I took 1885 as a year and put it in \"other\".\n- **Missing columns:** 92 Ardnamurchan has a value (I.) but no height, and no comma after the name. 105 Sanda has no value and no height.\n- **Values above V:** three stations are rated \"VI.\": 87 Ushenish, 98 Fladda and 104 Mull of Cantyre. The other reader's description of values as I–V is therefore incomplete.\n- **\"Character\" is null throughout:** the list gives values and heights, not light characters. No row has a type (L.H./L.V.) printed either.\n\nSpellings copied as printed: Rhu Stoir, Island Ghlais, Ushenish, Dhuheartach, Skervuile, Rhuvaal, Lochindaul, Mull of Cantyre, Devaar. \"M‘Arthur's Head\" is printed with a turned-comma M‘ and an ordinary apostrophe. The Diary text calls station 86 \"Monach Isles\", but the list has \"Monach Islands\".",
